var CHEAT=[{"t": "Descriptive statistics", "h": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"gbox\">mean = Σx / n                    median = middle value (average of the two middle ones if n is even)        mode = most frequent\nvariance σ² = Σ(x - x̄)² / N      std dev σ = √variance            range = max - min\nQ1 = median of the lower half    Q3 = median of the upper half    (median left out of both halves if n is odd)\nIQR = Q3 - Q1                    fences: Q1 - 1.5 x IQR   and   Q3 + 1.5 x IQR      (outside = outlier)\nfive-number summary = min, Q1, median, Q3, max\nz = (x - mean) / sd<\/pre>"}, {"t": "Estimation, confidence interval, hypothesis test", "h": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"gbox\">standard error  SE = s / √n\nconfidence interval = x̄ ± Z x s / √n          Z = 1.645 (90%)   1.96 (95%)   2.576 (99%)\nz-test:  z = (x̄ - μ) / (σ / √n)\nH0 always has the equality (=, ≤, ≥).   H1: μ &gt; value (right-tailed)   μ &lt; value (left-tailed)   μ ≠ value (two-tailed)\ncritical z at 5%: 1.645 one-tailed, 1.96 two-tailed.   |z| beyond critical  =&gt;  reject H0<\/pre>"}, {"t": "Correlation", "h": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"gbox\">Pearson   r = Σ(x - x̄)(y - ȳ) / √( Σ(x - x̄)² x Σ(y - ȳ)² )          -1 ≤ r ≤ +1\nSpearman  ρ = 1 - 6 Σd² / ( n (n² - 1) )          d = rank of x - rank of y\nties: share the average of the ranks they occupy (ranks 6 and 7  =&gt;  both 6.5)<\/pre>\n<div class=\"tbl scroll\"><table class=\"work\"><tr><th><\/th><th>r<\/th><th><\/th><th>Reading<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>0.8 - 1<\/td><td>very strong<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>0.6 - 0.8<\/td><td>strong<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>0.4 - 0.6<\/td><td>moderate<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>0.2 - 0.4<\/td><td>weak<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>0 - 0.2<\/td><td>very weak / none<\/td><\/tr><\/table><\/div>\n<p>Pearson = linear, uses values, sensitive to outliers. Spearman = monotonic, uses ranks, robust. Correlation is not causation.<\/p>"}, {"t": "Regression", "h": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"gbox\">simple linear   y = b0 + b1 x\nb1 = Σ(x - x̄)(y - ȳ) / Σ(x - x̄)²           b0 = ȳ - b1 x̄\nmultiple   y = b0 + b1 x1 + b2 x2 + ...          polynomial   y = b0 + b1 x + b2 x² + ...\nresidual e = y - ŷ           MSE = Σ(y - ŷ)² / N      RMSE = √MSE      MAE = Σ|y - ŷ| / N\nR² = 1 - Σ(y - ŷ)² / Σ(y - ȳ)²            closer to 1 = better fit\nlogistic    p = 1 / (1 + e^-z),   z = b0 + b1 x          class 1 if p ≥ 0.5<\/pre>\n<p>Table to draw: x, y, x - x̄, y - ȳ, product, (x - x̄)², each with a total.<\/p>"}, {"t": "KNN", "h": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"gbox\">d = √( (x1 - a1)² + (x2 - a2)² + ... )          Euclidean\nsteps: distance to every point -&gt; sort ascending -&gt; take K nearest -&gt; majority vote<\/pre>\n<p>Table: point, features, class, squared differences, distance, rank. Large-scale features dominate; scale them (min-max) when units differ.<\/p>"}, {"t": "K-means and hierarchical clustering", "h": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"gbox\">K-means: assign every point to its nearest centroid, then new centroid = mean of its points (x̄, ȳ); repeat until nothing moves\ndistortion (elbow method): plot against K, pick the bend\nsingle linkage   = MIN distance between members   (update the matrix with the minimum)\ncomplete linkage = MAX distance          average linkage = average of all pairwise distances\ncut the dendrogram: number of vertical lines the cut crosses = number of clusters<\/pre>"}, {"t": "Decision tree (ID3)", "h": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"gbox\">Entropy(S) = - Σ p log2 p                  0 = pure, 1 = two classes equally mixed\nGain(S, A) = Entropy(S) - Σ (|Sv| / |S|) x Entropy(Sv)        highest gain = root<\/pre>\n<div class=\"tbl scroll\"><table class=\"work\"><tr><th>Fractions<\/th><th>Entropy<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1/2, 1/2<\/td><td>1<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1/3, 2/3<\/td><td>0.918<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1/4, 3/4<\/td><td>0.811<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>2/5, 3/5<\/td><td>0.971<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>9/14, 5/14<\/td><td>0.940<\/td><\/tr><\/table><\/div>"}, {"t": "Confusion matrix (rows = actual, columns = predicted)", "h": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"gbox\">Accuracy    = (TP + TN) / total\nRecall      = TP / (TP + FN)          (sensitivity, TPR)\nPrecision   = TP / (TP + FP)\nSpecificity = TN / (TN + FP)\nF1-score    = 2 x P x R / (P + R)\nError rate  = (FP + FN) / total = 1 - accuracy\nFP = Type I error     FN = Type II error<\/pre>"}, {"t": "Recommender systems", "h": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"gbox\">cosine similarity   sim(a, b) = Σ ai bi / ( √Σ ai² x √Σ bi² )          1 = same direction, 0 = nothing in common\nTF = word count / total words      IDF = log(total docs / docs containing the word)      TF-IDF = TF x IDF\npredicted rating   R = Σ (sim x rating) / Σ sim          (weighted)      or the plain average of K neighbours\nPearson (centred cosine): subtract each user&#x27;s mean rating first\nMAE = Σ|actual - predicted| / n        RMSE = √( Σ(actual - predicted)² / n )\nhit rate = hits / users          ARHR = average of 1 / rank of the hits\ndiversity = 1 - average similarity of the recommended items\nhybrid: weighted a x CF + (1 - a) x CBF, switching, mixed, cascade, feature combination, feature augmentation, meta-level<\/pre>"}, {"t": "Ethics keywords", "h": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"gbox\">5 C&#x27;s: Consent, Confidentiality, Control, Compliance, Communication\nGDPR: purpose limitation, data minimisation, lawful basis, transparency and fairness, accuracy, storage limitation, integrity and confidentiality\nanonymisation techniques: suppression, generalisation, noise addition, differential privacy, k-anonymity\nbias types: historical, representation, measurement, algorithmic\nfairness: group (demographic parity), individual, equal opportunity\nfix bias: pre-processing (diverse data, reweighing), in-processing (constraints, adversarial), post-processing (audit, human in the loop, XAI)\naccountability: who (responsibility), how (auditability), the fix (redress)       LIME, SHAP = explainability<\/pre>"}, {"t": "Pandas one-liners", "h": "<div class=\"tbl scroll\"><table class=\"work\"><tr><th>Task<\/th><th>Command<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>read, look<\/td><td>pd.read_csv(&#x27;f.csv&#x27;), head(), tail(), shape, columns, dtypes, info(), describe(include=&#x27;all&#x27;)<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>select<\/td><td>df[&#x27;a&#x27;], df[[&#x27;a&#x27;,&#x27;b&#x27;]], df.iloc[2:6, 0], df.loc[mask, [&#x27;a&#x27;,&#x27;b&#x27;]]<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>filter<\/td><td>df[(df[&#x27;age&#x27;] &gt; 25) &amp; (df[&#x27;g&#x27;] == &#x27;F&#x27;)], df.query(&#x27;age &gt; 25 and cgpa &gt; 8&#x27;), between(50, 60)<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>missing<\/td><td>isnull().sum(), dropna(), fillna(0), fillna(df[&#x27;c&#x27;].mean()), ffill(), bfill(), interpolate()<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>new / change<\/td><td>df[&#x27;t&#x27;] = df[&#x27;a&#x27;] + df[&#x27;b&#x27;], apply(lambda m: ...), rename(columns={}), drop(columns=&#x27;a&#x27;, inplace=True)<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>order, group<\/td><td>sort_values(by=&#x27;a&#x27;, ascending=False), rank(), groupby(&#x27;d&#x27;)[&#x27;m&#x27;].mean(), reset_index(drop=True)<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>plots<\/td><td>plt.bar, plt.hist, plt.scatter, plt.boxplot, then plt.show()<\/td><\/tr><\/table><\/div>"}];
